From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: i8042 - give the sparc OF driver a name of its own

On sparc, i8042_platform_init() registers sparc_i8042_driver, a
platform driver that binds the firmware's "8042" node and reads the
port base and the two interrupts from its keyboard and mouse children.
It is named "i8042". When that probe finds both children,
i8042_platform_init() returns 0 with the driver still registered, and
i8042_init() then registers i8042_driver, also a platform driver named
"i8042". driver_register() refuses the second one:

  Error: Driver 'i8042' is already registered, aborting...

and i8042_init() gives up, so no sun4u machine with a PS/2 8042 and
both children gets a keyboard. (Without the mouse child the probe
returns -ENODEV first and the clash never shows.) The JavaStation path
doesn't register the OF driver and is not affected. Kernels that
still used platform_create_bundle() added the core's "i8042" platform
device first, the OF driver took it by name, and sparc_i8042_probe()
followed its NULL of_node: Debian 7's 3.2 panics there.

Name the OF driver "i8042-sparc". It matches by of_match_table, so
the name only has to differ from the core driver's.

Seen under QEMU's sun4u with OpenBIOS that has the 8042 kdmouse child
(wsh-pve openbios patch 0035, ps2-mouse? true): with this change the
keyboard registers ("serio: i8042 KBD port at
0x1fe02000060,0x1fe02000064") and evdev reports the keys.
---
 drivers/input/serio/i8042-sparcio.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/serio/i8042-sparcio.h b/drivers/input/serio/i8042-sparcio.h
--- a/drivers/input/serio/i8042-sparcio.h
+++ b/drivers/input/serio/i8042-sparcio.h
@@ -97,7 +97,7 @@
 
 static struct platform_driver sparc_i8042_driver = {
 	.driver = {
-		.name = "i8042",
+		.name = "i8042-sparc",
 		.of_match_table = sparc_i8042_match,
 	},
 	.probe		= sparc_i8042_probe,
